# Performance

- Choose collection types deliberately: `IEnumerable` for iteration-only, `IList`/`IReadOnlyList` when count or index access is needed
- Use `StringBuilder` for string concatenation inside loops
- Use `Span<T>` and `Memory<T>` for high-frequency operations on arrays/buffers
- Enable Lazy Loading only where explicitly required
- Use `AsNoTracking()` for read-only EF Core queries:

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — read-only query
var users = await _db.Users
    .AsNoTracking()
    .Where(u => u.IsActive)
    .ToListAsync(ct);
```
